      "title": "Sink rejections, by sink and reason",
      "description": "codexlb.selfobs.sink_rejections - exactly sink.Rejection, reused rather than duplicated (issue #8's explicit instruction). sink is one of loki|otlpmetric|otlptrace|agento11y (each Sink's own Name()); reason is one of sink.Reason* (line_too_long, out_of_order, stream_limit, rate_limited, unauthorized, bad_request, transport, too_old). Any nonzero reading here means a record that will never exist at its destination - this is what \"Loki rejections non-zero\" (dashboards/alerts/loki-rejections.yaml) now alerts on directly.",
